    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "And they are changing. America is now the biggest oil producer in history, and buys far less oil from the Gulf than it used to. Saudi Arabia's biggest customer today is China. In twenty twenty three, it was Beijing, not Washington, that brokered a deal restoring ties between Saudi Arabia and its old rival Iran. In twenty twenty four, Saudi Arabia's central bank joined In, a project that lets central banks settle payments directly in their own digital currencies, without touching the dollar. Beijing has been pushing to pay for more of its energy in its own currency, the yuan. And countries from Russia to India have settled some oil trades in currencies other than the dollar. The dollar's share of global reserves has slipped from about seventy one percent in the year two thousand to under sixty percent today.",
